Vita: when a game heap cannot allocate, the stack's code addresses are reported.

On this port a failed allocation in a JKRExpHeap stops the game (CRASH in do_alloc, upstream's
choice). The report names the heap, the size asked for and the free blocks, but not who asked.
Found by the whole-game sweep in Vita3K (13 Nov): the game heap, 24 MiB free of 27 in blocks of
13.2 and 9.1 MiB, asked for 0xCB20A0 bytes (13.3 MiB) on the restart after a fall in Faron
Woods, coming from the Forest Temple; the same numbers in every run. To find the caller, the
words on the stack that look like Thumb return addresses into the program are written as one
more error line before the stop. Diagnostic only: nothing changes unless an allocation fails.
Nothing changes outside TARGET_VITA.

--- a/libs/JSystem/src/JKernel/JKRExpHeap.cpp
+++ b/libs/JSystem/src/JKernel/JKRExpHeap.cpp
@@ -10,6 +10,9 @@
 #include "JSystem/JUtility/JUTConsole.h"
 #include "JSystem/JUtility/JUTException.h"
 #include <cstdlib>
+#if TARGET_VITA
+#include <cstdio>
+#endif
 
 JKRExpHeap* JKRExpHeap::createRoot(int maxHeaps, bool errorFlag) {
     JKRExpHeap* heap = NULL;
@@ -242,6 +245,26 @@
             OSReport_Error("%08X | %08X | %s\n", iter->getStartAddr(), iter->getEndAddr(), iter->getName());
         }
 
+#if TARGET_VITA
+        {
+            // Vita (patches/dusklight/0075): who asked. The words on the stack that look like
+            // Thumb return addresses into the program (odd, inside its code), oldest last: the
+            // call chain is among them (arm-vita-eabi-addr2line on the ELF names each).
+            volatile uintptr_t here = 0;
+            const uintptr_t* stack = (const uintptr_t*)&here;
+            char line[420];
+            int used = 0, found = 0;
+            line[0] = 0;
+            for (int i = 1; i < 640 && found < 36; ++i) {
+                const uintptr_t word = stack[i];
+                if ((word & 1) != 0 && word >= 0x81000000u && word < 0x81f00000u) {
+                    used += snprintf(line + used, sizeof(line) - used, "%08x ", (unsigned)word);
+                    ++found;
+                }
+            }
+            OSReport_Error("Code addresses on the stack: %s\n", line);
+        }
+#endif
         CRASH("Aborting due to allocation failure!");
     }
 #else
